	I have always been dissappointed in the size of levels in
nethack it would be great if the random dungeon generator would adapt
to the display size availiable, as to have some awesome HUGE levels...
I have also wondered why the game couldn't be changed as to allow
walking off the screen, which could be interesting, though probably
not as fun as simply fitting the game to a higher resolution text
mode...
	Also, maybe someone out there could share some info regarding
the chat command.. I have found little use for it, certainly much less
use compared to dip or loot. It would be nice if there was a say
command also.. it might be interesting to provide for some basic 
communication with mosters... It is a bit unrealistic that there would
be no way to suade a stupid orc to accept some money or food to leave
you alone or with some RND probability become tamed... 
	Another thing I don't understand is why I can polymorph my
pet to be a green dragon (eh! I got lucky) and to stay that way
while I seem to only retain the polymorph for a limited time...
This seems a bit inconsistant.. is there a way to avoid morphing
back to human form? (yuk!)
	As a final bombastic, self-indulgent, relly outta-hand
idea (being a concurrent LPmud-der) would it not be really neat
if a charater of a high level could somehow build his own level
that future generations of hackers would have to go through?
(It would chew up disk space.. but how much? It couldn't be
 that bad, and disk space is getting cheaper every day...)

	A mini-spoiler I found relevant to the recent shops
discussion... (kinda stupid, admittedly)

	Apparently an uncursed magic whistle will work well to
rob a shop in conjunction with a pet of course if applied while in
the doorway. I had no tripe rations, no knowledge of any teleport
scrolls, wands or have you so I let my pet rummage around in the
shop till it picked up something interesting... most of the time
the whistle would take the pet outside the doorway.

